::CW_U04_L06_Q01::Poem: The lantern kept a small sun in the room. Which paraphrase is best?{
~A. The lantern was actually the sun.#Incorrect. This treats figurative language literally.
=
~C. The room was outside at noon.#Incorrect. This changes the setting.
~D. The speaker hated light.#Incorrect. No evidence supports hate.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q02::Poem: The road folded behind us. Which interpretation is best supported?{
~B. The road is made of paper.#Incorrect. Folded is figurative.
~C. The speaker is at a party.#Incorrect. No evidence supports that.
~D. The road is brand new.#Incorrect. Age is not mentioned.
=
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q03::Poem: The blue cup waited beside the sink. Which is an accurate paraphrase?{
=
~A. A red plate broke in the cupboard.#Incorrect. This changes the details.
~C. The cup felt abandoned forever.#Incorrect. This is interpretation and overclaims.
~D. The sink was outdoors.#Incorrect. The poem does not say that.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q04::Poem: Her laugh opened every window. Which interpretation is best supported?{
~B. Her laugh repaired glass.#Incorrect. This treats figurative language literally.
~C. She works as a carpenter.#Incorrect. No evidence supports that.
=
~D. The windows are angry.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q05::Poem: The classroom emptied into afternoon. Which paraphrase is best?{
=
~B. The classroom became an ocean.#Incorrect. This invents a new image.
~C. Afternoon means the speaker is afraid.#Incorrect. That is unsupported interpretation.
~D. The classroom filled with midnight.#Incorrect. This contradicts afternoon.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q06::Poem: The letter slept unopened on the desk. Which interpretation is supported?{
~B. The letter is a person taking a nap.#Incorrect. Slept is personification.
~C. The desk is outside.#Incorrect. Not stated.
~D. The letter is already answered.#Incorrect. Unopened suggests the opposite.
=
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q07::Poem: The river carried pieces of sky. Which paraphrase is best?{
~B. The sky was broken into rocks.#Incorrect. This changes the image.
=
~C. The river carried luggage.#Incorrect. No luggage appears.
~D. The speaker is definitely flying.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q08::Poem: The house held its breath until the key turned. Which interpretation is best supported?{
~B. The house has lungs.#Incorrect. That is literalizing personification.
~C. The key disappeared.#Incorrect. The key turns.
=
~D. The house is underwater.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q09::Poem: The last note vanished into the rafters. Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~B. The singer became famous.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
~C. The roof collapsed.#Incorrect. Not stated.
~D. The note became a bird.#Incorrect. This changes the image.
=
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q10::Poem: The garden woke under rain. Which interpretation is best supported?{
=
~B. The garden literally opened its eyes.#Incorrect. Woke is figurative.
~C. The garden is dead forever.#Incorrect. Woke suggests life.
~D. The rain is made of stone.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q11::Poem: The empty swing nodded in the storm. Which paraphrase is best?{
~B. A child won a race.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
~C. The swing spoke a sentence.#Incorrect. Nodded is figurative movement.
=
~D. The storm ended before the poem began.#Incorrect. The storm is present.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q12::Poem: My shadow reached the door first. Which interpretation is best supported?{
~B. The speaker has no body.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
=
~C. The door is fake.#Incorrect. Not stated.
~D. The shadow buys a ticket.#Incorrect. Unsupported and literalized.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q13::Poem: The clock chewed the final minute. Which paraphrase is best?{
=
~B. A clock ate food.#Incorrect. Chewed is figurative.
~C. The minute became a sandwich.#Incorrect. This literalizes the image.
~D. The speaker ignored time.#Incorrect. The line focuses on time.
}

