~B. The street was cleaned with soap.#Incorrect. Erased is figurative.
~C. The speaker built a street.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
~D. The fog is colorful and loud.#Incorrect. Not stated.
=
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q15::Poem: The porch light trembled in the rain. Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~B. The porch ran away.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
~C. The rain became a lamp.#Incorrect. This changes meaning.
=
~D. The speaker is in a desert.#Incorrect. Contradicted by rain.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q16::Poem: The unopened gate leaned toward the road. Which interpretation is best supported?{
~B. The gate is definitely angry.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
=
~C. The road is indoors.#Incorrect. Not stated.
~D. The gate has disappeared.#Incorrect. The gate is present.
}

::CW_U04_L06_Q17::Poem: The winter field wore a white coat. Which paraphrase is best?{
~B. The field bought clothing.#Incorrect. This treats the metaphor literally.
~C. The field turned into a person.#Incorrect. Figurative language does not make it literal.
~D. The coat was in a closet.#Incorrect. Unsupported.
=
}

